WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.868
Some breaking news tonight.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:02.268
The former

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.837
president has missed a legal deadline

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.372
to turn documents over to the House

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:06.673
January six select committee.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.575
Senator Murray has latest, joins us now.

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.576
What do we know, sir?

00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:09.943
Well,

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:10.276
the committee

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.177
just put out a statement

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.612
saying that they have heard

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:13.680
from the former president

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.614
and his counsel

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.448
and essentially

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.182
they are giving him

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.217
a little bit more time

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.752
to begin producing these documents.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.319
They said

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.053
we have informed

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:21.521
Trump's counsel that he must begin

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:22.455
producing records

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.290
no later than next week,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.059
and he remains under subpoena

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:29.596
for testimony starting on November 14.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.230
So look,

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.531
in the past with other witnesses,

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.665
the committee has been willing

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.801
to push these document deadlines back.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.603
What is key is to have some engagement

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.138
going on behind the scenes.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:38.805
And it seems like,

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.173
at least at this point,

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:41.674
this is what's happening, Anderson.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.710
So what is the committee's next move?

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.544
And what happens?

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.280
So now we wait to see how this plays out.

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.114
You know, the committee said

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:48.848
by next week,

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.016
the Trump team has to start

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.017
producing documents.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:51.951
So we'll see

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.386
if there is some good faith effort

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:54.054
by the Trump team

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.321
to hand over some documents

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.322
or to at least say,

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:56.523
you know,

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.757
we can give you these documents,

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.892
but we have privilege concerns

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.993
about these others.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.928
Or we may see them continuing

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.830
to try to delay, delay, delay.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:03.963
You know,

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.331
we don't know if the Trump team

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:06.566
is going to try to be

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:07.233
in any way

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.501
cooperative with this committee

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.836
or if they could ultimately try

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:11.137
to file a lawsuit

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.005
or something like that

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:12.806
and essentially kick

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:13.807
the can down the road

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.375
because they expect the committee's work

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:17.310
to expire early on in January.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.344
We've asked the Trump team

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.479
repeatedly today

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:20.647
how they're going to play all of this,

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:21.948
and we have yet to hear back from them

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.716
Anderson. Sir Murray, appreciate it.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:24.150
Thank you.

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.151
Today's seen in The New York

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:26.686
Times and others, including Axios,

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:27.921
which broke the story,

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:28.388
are reporting

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:29.189
that the former president

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:29.622
could announce

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.890
another run sometime on

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.826
or around the 14th of this month.

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:33.993
Sources familiar with the matter

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.062
telling CNN that some of his top aides

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:38.064
consider this timeframe ideal

00:01:38.064 --> 00:01:40.100
if Republicans do well on Tuesday.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.401
As for the once and perhaps

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.335
future candidate,

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:43.203
here's what he said

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:44.971
yesterday at a rally in Iowa.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.275
I will very, very, very

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:51.377
probably do it again. Okay.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.313
Very angry.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.247
Get ready.

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:56.783
That's all I'm telling you very soon.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:01:58.151
Get ready.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.420
Get ready.

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.921
Joining us now, CNN political analyst,

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:02.722
New York Times senior

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:04.624
political correspondent Maggie Haberman.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.225
She is, of course,

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:05.925
the bestselling

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.560
author of the remarkable book

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.394
Confidence Man

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.629
The Making of Donald Trump

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.598
and the Breaking of America.

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:12.599
So, Maggie, how real is

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.300
I mean, this is happening. This is real.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.535
What are you hearing?

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.470
It It sure seems, though, Anderson.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:18.171
Look, with Donald Trump,

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:19.672
you never want to say it's an absolute.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.407
Jonathan Swan of Vaccines

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:22.642
was careful not to.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:23.443
But I have been hearing

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:24.277
from multiple people

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:24.878
that it's likely

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.480
to be that week of November 14th.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.948
They considered an ideal time,

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:29.649
as you said,

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:30.517
because it would be right

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.417
after the midterms.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.852
He had been talking about announcing

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.087
before the midterms

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.089
that really worried a lot of Republicans

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.590
who tried to talk him out of it

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.092
through various methods, telling him

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:39.626
he would be,

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.561
you know, blamed if they lost.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:42.629
Remember,

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:43.863
he loses some things

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:44.998
by doing this, Anderson.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.166
What he thinks he gains

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.400
is some protection

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.135
from Justice Department investigations

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.236
and he tries to forestall

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.070
the rest of the field,

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:52.272
especially in a week

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:52.906
that Mike Pence,

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:55.341
his book is coming out when he loses

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.376
is the ability

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.677
to use his outside groups

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.945
to pay for legal bills.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.080
The clock starts on his hard

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.015
dollar fundraising

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.183
and hard dollar spending.

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.951
So it's not without risks.

00:03:04.951 --> 00:03:05.318
But, you know,

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:06.553
he has been out of the limelight

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:07.954
in a way that he can't stand.

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.722
And I think that's a big piece of this.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:12.192
Is that what I mean is that would tip

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:13.026
the scale, you think?

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.528
I think would tip the scale.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:16.729
Is always with him

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.865
getting attention is the biggest deal.

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.800
I think that wanting to freeze the field

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.101
and wanting to send a signal

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:23.136
to the Justice Department

00:03:23.136 --> 00:03:24.470
that he is going to make it as hard

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.573
as possible on them publicly

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:27.574
should they move ahead

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:28.875
with any kind of indictment of him

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.043
or in Georgia

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.245
of any will as investigation.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.646
That's a state investigation.

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.582
I think that all of these are factors

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.383
I don't think one necessarily outweighs

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.051
the other,

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:39.986
but I think that he has always thought

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.821
that getting in sooner rather than later

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:42.689
made more sense.

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:43.489
Do you know

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:43.623
I mean,

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.858
do you have a sense of what his campaign

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.728
will look like at this stage or I mean,

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.730
is it going to be these big rallies?

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.232
Does he have staff?

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:54.834
It's a really good question.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:55.802
And the answer on staff

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.470
is it's pretty lean right now.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.871
And, you know, folks around

00:03:58.871 --> 00:04:00.406
him will say that's by design

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:01.808
because they consider 20, 20

00:04:01.808 --> 00:04:02.976
to be fairly bloated.

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:04.811
But it's also frankly

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:07.213
reflecting the reality that so far

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.248
and in some cases it's

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:09.148
because people are tied up

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:09.949
with the midterms.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:10.683
In some cases,

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.985
there are people who are very leery

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:12.752
of getting involved

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:13.753
in Donald Trump's orbit

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.188
because of the constant churn

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:17.490
around him, legal and otherwise.

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.058
And so I think it will be small

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:19.559
at least

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.227
going into early 2023

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:22.695
assuming he does get in.

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:25.198
I think you will see some small number

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:26.099
of political events

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.700
happening after he declares

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.101
we don't know

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.003
the declaration would be a rally

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.304
or if it would be a press conference.

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:32.639
And I think they're looking at both.

00:04:32.639 --> 00:04:34.107
But then I think he will resume rallies

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.141
the way he had before

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.109
I don't think you're going to see him

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:38.144
suddenly become a retail politician.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:38.911
He's never liked it.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:39.846
He's never been good at it,

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.547
and I don't think he thinks he needs to.

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:42.849
You just heard Sara

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.050
Murray is reporting that former

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.752
president missed the subpoena deadline

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.586
to provide documents,

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:47.887
the General Ethics Committee.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.423
Would an announcement complicate

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.892
any potential dealings with.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:54.627
I guess it would complicate any dealings

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:55.228
with the committee?

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:57.430
Well, I don't

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.531
know that it complicates it.

00:04:58.531 --> 00:04:59.432
I mean, I think it's certainly become

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:01.100
something else that he points to.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:01.801
I think Donald Trump

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:02.835
is running out the clock

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:03.970
because he thinks that the committee

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.305
is going to go away

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:06.606
if a House

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:07.607
majority is given

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:09.475
to Republicans after next Tuesday,

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:10.510
which at the moment

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.012
polling indicates it most likely will be.

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:13.713
It's just not clear

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.648
what the margin will be if that happens.

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:17.650
But his assumption is and his aides

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.451
assumption is

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.886
this is going to at some point

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:21.187
end in the Sara said,

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:22.221
I think they have to decide

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:23.790
whether they want to file a lawsuit

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.125
to just help stall that that motion.

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:27.327
Do you think he would

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:28.227
hold his announcement

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:29.262
even if the Georgia election

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:30.530
results are still undecided?

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:32.632
Well, I do,

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:32.865
but I

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:34.233
think that he will be under pressure

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:34.834
not to.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:35.902
And we'll see what happens

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:36.769
if there is a runoff.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:37.970
I think that is absolutely

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.272
a complicating factor.

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.074
You know, he is already being blamed,

00:05:41.074 --> 00:05:42.542
continues to be blamed

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.911
for the losses in Georgia on January 5th.

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:47.013
2021 in those runoffs.

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.948
I'm not sure that anyone around him

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:50.016
thinks it's a wise idea

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:51.584
for him to face that again.

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:52.852
Do you think

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:56.055
he announces does he then get

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.091
I guess then he sort of

00:05:58.091 --> 00:05:58.358
I mean,

00:05:58.358 --> 00:05:59.592
I don't know how much coverage he's

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:02.862
been getting on, you know, a Fox News or

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.264
you know, big conservative outlet.

00:06:05.264 --> 00:06:06.632
Does that.

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:09.836
Does that make him more more bookable

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:11.471
on those shows?

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:13.706
I think it's a problem for him, Anderson.

00:06:13.706 --> 00:06:14.941
I think for a number of reasons,

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:15.808
the conservative media

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.410
landscape has changed for him.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.711
I think one major reason

00:06:18.711 --> 00:06:19.846
is that so

00:06:19.846 --> 00:06:20.880
many of these outlets

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.781
have gotten embroiled

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:22.982
in defamation lawsuits

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.450
by election companies

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.418
because of the

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:27.720
the lies about the election in 20, 20

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:29.922
that were spouted on their platforms

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:31.190
or on their on their websites

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.325
or in their programs.

00:06:32.325 --> 00:06:34.761
And I think that there is some risk

00:06:34.761 --> 00:06:36.596
in their minds in having him on,

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:36.863
you know,

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:38.598
but he has very visibly

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:40.700
not been on Fox News very much.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.201
He's not on Newsmax.

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:42.502
You know,

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:43.503
he is really relegated

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:44.937
to, you know, other podcasts

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:47.006
or some conservative radio.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:48.474
It's just a very different world

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:49.542
than it was in 20, 15

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.277
when he first got into politics.

00:06:51.277 --> 00:06:51.844
Interesting point.

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:52.812
Maggie Haberman, appreciate it.

00:06:52.812 --> 00:06:53.179
Thank you.

